  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n\n\n**\n¶2:**\n When\n the Divine\n Human\n went forth to\n cont\nend against\n evil\n,\n it\n clothed itself in the ou\ntermost expression\n of celestial love —\n love\n made\n active\n and militant\n. By\n means\n of this surrounding\n truth\n of\n living\n love\n, it collapsed\n the sw\nelling pride\n of evil;\n it cast\n down the ins\nanity and emptiness of falsity\n.\n\n\n**¶3:** Now\n, this celest\nial love alone would\n have\n been sufficient against\n all\n evil.\n Yet\n because\n love by\n itself,\n when\n it makes\n contact\n with the opposition\n of evil\n, is rendered\n vulnerable\n —\n for\n love without supporting truths can\n be ass\nailed —\n therefore\n four\n further\n protecting\n tru\nths were joined\n to it: the truth\n of spiritual\n understanding\n, the truth of rational\n cogn\nition, the truth of wisdom in\n its intellig\nible form, and the truth of in\nmost innocence.\n And\n why\n were\n these four given\n? They\n were given so that they\n would\n serve\n and\n guard\n celest\nial love;\n so that evil and\n falsity could not penetrate into the\n interior\n of love\n itself, and so that the poison and\n \nenmity of hell\n could not sever love\n from\n its\n source.\n\n**¶4:**\n Celest\nial love indeed\n received\n injury\n in\n its ou\ntermost form through its\n contact with evil —\n yet\n even\n so\n, all\n the powers\n of fals\nity were\n held\n at\n bay by its\n presence. And\n it\n was necessary\n that the\n allied\n fac\nulties,\n its\n companion\n qualities\n, should also\n receive injury and be\n infilt\nrated by the power\n of evil. The\n nature\n of evil became\n com\nmingled with them\n all\n —\n except with\n in\nmost innocence.\n Fals\nity could not mix\n with innoc\nence, nor could the\n consuming\n self\n-love of evil penetrate into\n it\n.\n\n**¶5:** Nevertheless\n, even that\n one\n quality\n which\n remained unw\nounded —\n which is inmost innocence — div\nested itself of its own ou\ntermost truth\n and its\n own capacity, and best\nowed these\n freely\n upon its four companion\n faculties,\n so that by\n the\n surrounding\n truth of innoc\nence they would\n be made\n strong, and would\n end\nure, and would be\n sustained\n in\n their work\n. And innoc\nence became for\n them their\n very\n life.",
